{
 "annotations": {
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Site KPI summary"
 },
 "description": "Return headline KPIs (revenue, sessions, RPS, AOV, CVR), engagement metrics, current and previous daily trends with cumulative revenue, bot-excluded session count (null with a note when that count cannot be retrieved), period_observation_status, and ad-spend availability / Path A/B context for a site and period. Revenue-dependent metrics and trend revenue are null unless purchase measurement is confirmed; null means unverified, not zero. When a confirmed period has no traffic, period_observation_status is no_observation and current revenue, RPS, AOV, and CVR are null; observed zero revenue remains numeric zero. A missing revenue history alone does not show that purchase measurement is unconfigured. When revenue is unverified, explain that sales are unverified and guide the user to check purchase measurement; do not claim it is not set up. On a required current-data retrieval failure, the tool returns isError=true, revenue_status='error', revenue=null and error_code='retrieval_failed'; never read it as zero. A previous-window RPC failure keeps current data and makes comparison_status unavailable, with previous KPI/trend fields null. Trend conversions is an observed purchase-event count and is not a confirmation of revenue measurement. Paid Attribution ROAS is unavailable; kpis.roas remains null for response compatibility and must not be presented as a measured ROAS. Sessions and engagement metrics remain available independently. AOV and RPS are null when their denominator is zero. Use optional country (ISO2, e.g. 'JP') and/or device ('mobile'/'desktop'/'tablet') to scope session-derived metrics. site_id is optional when OAuth-authenticated. Default period is the last 30 days; pass period='today'/'7d'/'90d' or a raw day count (1-365). For exact calendar dates in the site's analysis time zone, pass start_date and end_date, optionally with comparison dates. Revenue/sessions/RPS/AOV/avg_duration change is percentage or null when the prior value is zero; CVR and bounce_rate change is a percentage-point delta.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "compare_end_date": {
    "$ref": "#/properties/start_date"
   },
   "compare_start_date": {
    "$ref": "#/properties/start_date"
   },
   "country": {
    "maxLength": 2,
    "minLength": 2,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "device": {
    "enum": [
     "mobile",
     "desktop",
     "tablet"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "end_date": {
    "$ref": "#/properties/start_date"
   },
   "period": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "const": "today",
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "const": "7d",
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "const": "30d",
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "const": "90d",
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "maximum": 365,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
     }
    ],
    "default": "30d"
   },
   "site_id": {
    "format": "uuid",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "start_date": {
    "pattern": "^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
